# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Generated content.
#
# The rule here is: DATASETS and BINARIES are not published; EVIDENCE is.
#
# Artifacts and the governance trail are the whole argument this project makes
# ("the result is reproducible and the choice is documented"), so they are
# tracked. A repository that ignored them would ask a reader to take that
# argument on trust, which is exactly the failure the project exists to fix.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Datasets are never redistributed. The pipeline downloads them, or the user
# supplies their own. This pattern matches data/ at ANY depth, so it covers
# workspaces/<slug>/data/ too.
data/
!data/**/.gitkeep

# Regenerable CSV analysis output.
results/
!results/**/.gitkeep

# Run logs are noise and churn on every execution.
logs/

# Trained model binaries are Python pickles, which execute arbitrary code when
# loaded. Publishing them invites a supply-chain problem for anyone who forks
# and loads one. The pipeline regenerates them in seconds, and their
# metadata.json plus model_registry.json - the actual evidence of what was
# trained and chosen - ARE tracked.
*.joblib

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Workspaces.
# Only the graded churn project is published. The remaining workspaces are
# throwaway upload smoke-tests, and one of them (california-housing-sample-9)
# carries a misleading R2 of 0.926 against a `latitude` target that would be
# read as a headline result out of context.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
workspaces/*
!workspaces/churn/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Web application build output.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
node_modules/
.next/
.next-verify/
webapp/.uploads/

# Generated GitHub Pages output.
_site/

# Local agent tooling state - not part of the project.
.claude-flow/
